# The public tree is `git archive` of a ref with these honoured.
# The private chat follower and its test stay in the repo but out of the export.
# The follower lives in private/, which is no package in pyproject, so no wheel
# can carry it however it is built; MANIFEST.in keeps it out of the sdist.
# Both lines: `private` drops the directory from git archive (else an empty
# `private/` entry is left), and `private/**` marks each file inside, since an
# attributes pattern on a directory does not reach its files (gitattributes(5)).
private export-ignore
private/** export-ignore
tests/test_follower.py export-ignore
# openspec/ is the private design record: out of the export, kept in the repo
# (as sessionmail does with its own). Both lines, for the reason given above.
openspec export-ignore
openspec/** export-ignore
tests/test_host_literal.py export-ignore
